{
  "analysis": "Doom boots and loads the WAD, but fails at R_Init with Z_Malloc trying to allocate 25MB. DEFAULT_RAM is 6 MiB, so the zone should be 6MB. The output says \"600000 allocated for zone\" - I need to determine if this is hex (0x600000 = 6MB, correct) or decimal (600000 = ~586KB, too small). The 25MB allocation attempt is suspicious and likely indicates an interpreter bug producing incorrect values. I need to search for the zone memory printf format string and investigate the R_Init allocation.",
  "plan": "Search for the \"zone memory\" and \"allocated for zone\" strings in the source/binary to determine if the size is printed in hex or decimal. Then inspect R_Init/R_InitTextures to understand what causes the 25MB allocation. Also check for potential interpreter bugs in load/store or arithmetic instructions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -rn \"zone memory\\|allocated for zone\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/*.c /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/*.h | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "strings /app/doomgeneric_mips | grep -i \"zone memory\\|allocated for zone\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"R_Init\\|R_InitTextures\\|R_InitColormaps\\|R_InitData\\|Z_Malloc\\|malloc\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/r_data.c | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"R_Init\\|R_InitTextures\\|R_InitColormaps\\|R_InitData\\|R_InitPointToAngle\\|R_InitTables\" /app/doomgeneric/doomgeneric/r_main.c | head -30\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
